\begin{abstract}
We present a unified cosmological framework in which spacetime geometry,
gravitational curvature, and early supermassive black hole formation emerge
from the dynamics of a Primordial Informational Field (PIF). Using the
Quantum-Informational Astrophysics Simulation Engine (QIA-SE v9.4), we derive
the Informational Field Equation (IFE), the Emergent Metric Equation (EME),
and the SMBH Informational Sink Equation (SISE). Stress testing across
Planck-scale curvature, non-linear informational gradients, and super-Eddington
accretion demonstrates numerical stability, UV regularization, and observational
compatibility with Planck CMB and JWST high-redshift quasar data.
\end{abstract}

